  "description": "Ibn Sina's short treatise on the soul, in ten sections: the existence of the spiritual faculties, their division, the vegetative and animal powers, the five senses, the inward senses, and the argument that the soul is an immaterial substance. It is a compact route into the psychology that Avicenna's Latin readers inherited.",
